'''Old Welsh''' ({{langx|cy|Hen Gymraeg}}) is the stage of the [[Welsh language]] from about 800 AD until the early 12th century when it developed into [[Middle Welsh]].{{sfnp|Koch|2006|p=1757}} The preceding period, from the time Welsh became distinct from [[Common Brittonic]] around 550, has been called "Primitive"{{sfnp|Koch|2006|p=1757}} or "Archaic Welsh".{{sfnp|Willis|2009|p=1}}

